---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout description="Mat builds the boring parts that keep AI agents alive — permissions, recovery, and evals.">
  <section class="home-hero site-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="hero-kicker">DEVELOPER / BUILDER / LEARNER</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Less magic.<br /><em>More runtime.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-description">I build the boring parts that keep AI agents alive —<br class="desktop-break" /> permissions, recovery, and evals.</p>
      <p class="hero-disciplines">RUNTIME <span>/</span> TOOLS <span>/</span> RECOVERY <span>/</span> EVALS <span>/</span> RELIABLE SYSTEMS</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-structure" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="structure-slab structure-slab-back"></div>
      <div class="structure-slab structure-slab-front"></div>
      <div class="structure-opening"></div>
      <span class="structure-caption">FORM FOLLOWS FUNCTION — 001</span>
    </div>
    <span class="hero-index" aria-hidden="true">01 / 03</span>
  </section>

  <aside class="now-strip site-shell" aria-label="Currently building">
    <span class="now-label">NOW</span>
    <span class="now-current"><span class="mint-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Building Relay</span>
    <span class="now-description">Durable execution for long-running agents.</span>
  </aside>

  <section class="work-section site-shell" id="work" aria-labelledby="selected-work">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-index">01 / WORK</p>
      <h2 id="selected-work">Selected work<span class="mint-period">.</span></h2>
      <p>Systems for the moments<br />when software must hold.</p>
    </div>
    <article class="featured-project">
      <div class="featured-copy">
        <span class="project-number">01 / FEATURED PROJECT</span>
        <h3>AgentPermit4j</h3>
        <p class="project-tagline">Guardrails for the part of an agent that can actually break things.</p>
        <p class="project-description">A trusted action execution layer for Java agents. It places authorization, risk policy, exact-call approval, idempotency, and audit between a proposed action and the code that executes it.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/mat973252/agent-permit4j" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture" role="img" aria-label="Proposed action flows through policy, approval, execution, and audit">
        <span class="diagram-label">THE ACTION BOUNDARY</span>
        <ol>
          <li><span>01</span>Proposal</li>
          <li><span>02</span>Policy</li>
          <li><span>03</span>Approval</li>
          <li><span>04</span>Execute</li>
          <li><span>05</span>Audit</li>
        </ol>
        <span class="diagram-foot">CONTROL BEFORE CONSEQUENCE</span>
      </div>
      <p class="project-metadata">JAVA 21 <span>/</span> SPRING AI <span>/</span> POLICY <span>/</span> APPROVAL</p>
    </article>
    <div class="secondary-projects">
      <article class="secondary-project">
        <span class="project-number">02 / EXPERIMENTAL</span>
        <div>
          <h3>RAGContract4j</h3>
          <p class="secondary-tagline">Make bad retrieval fail CI, not production.</p>
          <p>Turns retrieval, authorization, and citation requirements into repeatable quality gates.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="project-arrow" href="https://github.com/mat973252/rag-contract4j" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View RAGContract4j on GitHub">↗</a>
      </article>
      <article class="secondary-project">
        <span class="project-number">03 / TOOL</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Claude Recovery Hooks</h3>
          <p class="secondary-tagline">Claude died.<br />The task didn't have to.</p>
          <p>PowerShell hooks for recovering Claude Code sessions after transient upstream failures.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="project-arrow" href="https://github.com/mat973252/claude-recovery-hooks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View Claude Recovery Hooks on GitHub">↗</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="post-section site-shell" id="notes" aria-labelledby="latest-posts">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-index">02 / NOTES</p>
      <h2 id="latest-posts">Field notes<span class="mint-period">.</span></h2>
      <p>Writing on agents,<br />systems, and what lasts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="notes-columns" aria-hidden="true"><span>DATE</span><span>TITLE / DESCRIPTION</span><span>READ</span></div>
    <a class="note-entry" href="/posts/agent-anchor/">
      <time datetime="2026-08-30">30 AUG 2026</time>
      <span class="note-content"><strong>Agent 时代下的锚点</strong><span>从 Java 后端与企业知识检索实践出发，梳理 Agent 从 Demo 走向生产环境时不会轻易过时的八类工程能力。</span></span>
      <span class="note-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
